<title>GERMANY: Hamburg air cargo falls 4.5 pct in February.</title>
<headline>Hamburg air cargo falls 4.5 pct in February.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Hamburg airport (HAM) in February fell 4.5 percent to 2,922 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>This followed a fractional rise of 0.8 percent in January, the monthly ADV traffic report added.</p>
<p>The following tables show 1997 details with all figures in tonnes and percentage changes on the same period 12 months ago.</p>
<p>    Feb 1997			Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		2,922		Down 4.5</p>
<p>    Exports			    1,153		Down 6.9</p>
<p>    Imports			    1,766		Down 2.3</p>
<p>    Transit				  3		     n/a</p>
<p>    Jan-Feb 1997		 Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		5,640		Down 2.0</p>
<p>    Exports			    2,223		Down 4.7</p>
<p>    Imports			    3,411		Up   0.3</p>
<p>    Transit				  6		     n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
